BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movie-1005402@doc-radar
DTSTAMP:20260917T204334Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Fragments of Paradise
DESCRIPTION:Directed by KD Davison\n\nFor over 70 years\, Jonas Mekas\, i
 nternationally known as the "godfather" of avant-garde cinema\, document
 ed his life in what came to be known as his diary films. From his arriva
 l in New York City as a displaced person in 1949 to his death in 2019\, 
 he chronicled the trauma and loss of exile while pioneering institutions
  to support the growth of independent film in the United States. Fragmen
 ts of Paradise is an intimate look at his life and work constructed from
  thousands of hours of his own video and film diaries-including never-be
 fore-seen tapes and unpublished audio recordings. It is a story about fi
 nding beauty amidst profound loss\, and a man who tried to make sense of
  it all... with a camera.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1005402
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1005402
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
