SUMMARY:Remake (PBS (POV & Independent Lens))
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Ross McElwee\n\nFrom PBS (POV & Independent Lens)
 \n\nFor nearly forty years\, Ross McElwee has made autobiographical docu
 mentaries about how his personal life intersects with the wider world. A
 fter his son Adrian died of a fentanyl overdose in 2016\, McElwee abando
 ned a planned Hollywood dramatic remake of his own 1986 breakthrough fil
 m Sherman's March\, and instead used decades of home-movie footage — i
 ncluding Adrian's own camera work — to reckon with his son's life\, hi
 s addiction\, and what the camera did and did not capture.\n\nhttps://ww
 w.themoviedb.org/tv/14955/season/39/episode/6
