SUMMARY:Secrets of the Bayeux Tapestry: Inside the Museum
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Joe Myerscough\n\nThe Bayeux Tapestry is one of t
 he treasures of the medieval world. Across 70 metres of exquisitely embr
 oidered scenes\, it tells the story of one of the most seismic events in
  British history – the Norman Invasion of 1066.  For the last 950 year
 s\, this crucial part of Britain's national story has remained on the ot
 her side of the English Channel\, in Bayeux\, Normandy\, but now it’s 
 coming back to the UK.  A stellar cast of historians and experts follow 
 the painstaking efforts to bring this priceless work of art back to the 
 UK\, where experts believe it was made\, for a once-in-a-millennium exhi
 bition at the British Museum.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/176984
 4
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1769844
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
