SUMMARY:1 in 2
DESCRIPTION:Directed by David Wilkinson\n\nNearly one in two of us will b
 e diagnosed with cancer at some point in our lives. David Nicholas Wilki
 nson is one of them\, twice over. In 2020\, a colonoscopy found his bowe
 l to be extremely healthy for a man his age. In 2023\, a FIT test came b
 ack clear and\, like almost everyone who takes one\, he assumed that mea
 nt the all-clear. In 2024\, a second colonoscopy found bowel cancer. Sta
 ge 4. He was told his tumour was 5-6 years old. What went wrong? A FIT t
 est looks for blood. Wilkinson’s tumour never bled. Nor do a great man
 y others.  1 IN 2 follows Wilkinson through his own treatment\, where he
  discovers a steep rise in bowel cancer among people far too young to be
  screened for it\, and far too young\, it seems\, to be believed. Among 
 those who tell him their stories is a bowel surgeon whose own symptoms w
 ere dismissed by her oncologist colleagues and in part by herself becaus
 e she was only 44.\n\nhttps://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1771402
URL:https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/1771402
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
